{"step_index":750,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T01:49:22Z","content":"The files have been updated so that **every single mission displays its actual in-game storyline title** alongside its internal engine codename.\n\n---\n\n### Key Updates Applied Across the Project\n\n#### 1. [`output/mission_order.json`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/output/mission_order.json)\n* Populated the `display_name` field for all 97 replay missions and table variants with their in-game storyline titles (e.g., `INT_PROLO` $\\rightarrow$ *\"Prologue (Counselor Interview)\"*, `INT_CHASE` $\\rightarrow$ *\"Gone Fishing (Boat Drop)\"*, `FT_KMODSHP` $\\rightarrow$ *\"Just a Scratch (Ganado Repair)\"*, `BAN_FINAL` $\\rightarrow$ *\"THE CARTEL HEIST\"*, `AIR_FINAL` $\\rightarrow$ *\"VCIA TAKEDOWN\"*, `BIL_PENT` $\\rightarrow$ *\"FINAL STANDOFF\"*, `BIL_FINAL_B` $\\rightarrow$ *\"Ending B: The Deal\"*, etc.).\n\n#### 2. [`output/mission_flow.mmd`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/output/mission_flow.mmd)\n* Every flowchart node now prominently showcases the **bold in-game mission name** on line 1, followed by the internal code ID on line 2, and its architectural role on line 3:\n  ```mermaid\n  m_INT_CHASE[\"<b>Gone Fishing (Boat Drop)</b><br/><code>INT_CHASE</code> • <i>Main Story Core</i>\"]:::coreStory\n  m_FT_KMODSHP[\"<b>Just a Scratch (Ganado Repair)</b><br/><code>FT_KMODSHP</code> • <i>Mandatory Gate</i>\"]:::branching\n  m_BAN_FINAL[\"<b>THE CARTEL HEIST (Sinfrontera Vault Raid)</b><br/><code>BAN_FINAL</code> • <i>Chapter 3 Climax Bottleneck</i>\"]:::bottleneck\n  m_AIR_FINAL[\"<b>VCIA TAKEDOWN (Airport Cargo Heist)</b><br/><code>AIR_FINAL</code> • <i>Chapter 4 Climax Bottleneck</i>\"]:::bottleneck\n  m_BIL_PENT[\"<b>FINAL STANDOFF (Key West Penthouse)</b><br/><code>BIL_PENT</code> • <i>Confrontation Decision Gate</i>\"]:::bottleneck\n  ```\n\n#### 3. [`output/SPEEDRUN_ROUTING_NOTES.md`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/output/SPEEDRUN_ROUTING_NOTES.md)\n* Section 2 provides a complete, 5-chapter master directory table aligning:\n  * **In-Game Mission Name**\n  * **Internal Engine ID**\n  * **Narrative Strand / Category**\n  * **Speedrun Classification / Routing Advisory**\n\n---\n\n### Campaign Overview with In-Game Titles\n\n| Chapter | Sequential Scope | Key Story Bottlenecks (In-Game Names) | Core Heists & Climax Operations |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise** *(Leonida Keys)* | Missions 1 – 22 | **Prologue** $\\rightarrow$ **Gone Fishing** $\\rightarrow$ **Gear Up** $\\rightarrow$ **Just a Scratch** $\\rightarrow$ **Coming Home** $\\rightarrow$ **Buck Me** | **Doin' Gone** (Trailer Climax leading into Chapter 2) |\n| **Chapter 2: Paradise Lost** *(Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)* | Missions 23 – 35 | **What's in the Bag?** $\\rightarrow$ **Moses** $\\rightarrow$ **Hit Kingpin Bowling** | **Checking Out** (Starlet Motel Evacuation Climax) |\n| **Chapter 3: Syndicate Expansion** *(Vice City Metro)* | Missions 36 – 65 | **Welcome to Vice City** $\\rightarrow$ **Car Service** $\\rightarrow$ **Sinfrontera Bank Scope** | **THE CARTEL HEIST** ($10.5M Sinfrontera Vault Raid) |\n| **Chapter 4: Airport Takedown** *(Ocean Beach & VCIA)* | Missions 66 – 90 | **Ocean Beach** $\\rightarrow$ **Party Hard** ($75k Wire Gate) $\\rightarrow$ **Close Surveillance** | **VCIA TAKEDOWN** (Airport Cargo Heist) $\\rightarrow$ **Sunset** (Point of No Return) |\n| **Chapter 5: Top of the World, Ma!** *(The Climax)* | Missions 91 – 97 | **Top of the World** $\\rightarrow$ **FINAL STANDOFF** (Key West Penthouse) | **Ending A: Bonnie & Clyde** ($2M Payout) *or* **Ending B: The Deal** (Speedrun Bypass) $\\rightarrow$ **Final Evacuation** |\n\n*All updated files have been synced directly to [`C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads`](file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads).*","thinking":"Each node now displays the in-game mission name, formatted in bold, representing the current active mission associated with that game state. This consistent display across all nodes confirms successful retrieval and formatting of the mission data.\n\n\n"}
